You may only use the obtained data and information (hereinafter collectively referred to as the "data") at your own risk and responsibility. The report was generated based on the current information in the Central Register of Vehicles (CEP).

The data in the CEP register may not reflect the actual state of affairs, as, among others:

 · data collected in the Central Register of Vehicles are being provided under various procedures and within various time frames, by various means by relevant responsible institutions, such as, for example vehicle registration authorities, vehicle inspection stations and the Police.;
 · In principle, the Minister of Digital Affairs is not entitled to independently: check, enter, supplement, update, change or delete the collected data. ;
 · and data in CEP may be affected by circumstances related to their collection processes (such as acts of force majeure, the quality of remote data transmission services, data transfer deadlines, etc.).

The legal basis: art. 80a para. 2 and Art. 80cb para. 1 and 3 of the Act of June 20, 1997. The Road Traffic Law (consolidated text - Journal of Laws of 2020, item 110) of 2020, item 110).

